{title: Sound the Battle Cry}
{artist: William F. Sherwin}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Upbeat}
{flow: Closing}
{key: A}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 110}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Source: Praise and Victory Songs, by Homer A. Rodeheaver & Harry D. Clarke (Chicago, Illinois: Rodeheaver Company, 1932), # 30)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Sound the battle cry! [D]See, the [A]foe is nigh;
[E]Raise the standard high [B7]for the [E]Lord;
[A]Gird your armor on, [D]stand firm [A]every one;
[A]Rest your [F#m]cause upon His [E7]holy [A]Word.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[A]Rouse, then, soldiers, [E7]rally round the [A]banner,
[C#]Ready, [F#m]steady, [B]pass the word a__[E]__long;
[A]Onward, forward, [E7]shout aloud Ho[A]sanna!
[A]Christ is [F#m]captain of the [E7]mighty [A]throng.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]Strong to meet the foe, [D]marching [A]on we go,
[E]While our cause we know, [B7]must pre[E]vail;
[A]Shield and banner bright, [D]gleaming [A]in the light,
[A]Battling [F#m]for the right we [E7]ne’er can [A]fail.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]O! Thou God of all, [D]hear us [A]when we call,
[E]Help us one and all [B7]by Thy [E]grace;
[A]When the battle’s done, [D]and the [A]vict’ry’s won,
[A]May we [F#m]wear the crown be[E7]fore Thy [A]face.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
